{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>My flesh and my heart fail</b> — this is the body." "<b>And my heart</b> — this is the desiring soul, which is the faculty of generation. Only <b>the rock of my heart</b> is like the meaning of <b>my strength</b>, and <b>my heart</b> in the manner of: <b>after your hearts and after your eyes</b>. And the meaning of <b>the rock of my heart</b> is the bond that endures forever and does not perish; therefore [it says] <b>this</b> after it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {1 "The verse cited in full reads 'my flesh and my heart fail, but God is the rock of my heart and my portion forever'; 'this' refers to the word 'forever' (לעולם) that follows."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:21.046874226Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}